mesg "Title: The stepsFrom:  LiliaDate:  Sat Sep 141. Install SunOS 4.1.42. remove ALL services in /etc/inetd.conf   you may remove the network cable if you wish3. rebuild kernel if you like4. upgrade system to C2 level, see reference manual5. install SNP ptelnet on port 236. install tcp-wrapper & identd7. if no one need mail, get rid of sendmail8. install wu-ftpd9. remount mudlib, reopenThat's the abstract. I am not going to do this myself 'cause this processspends me up to two or three more workdays. However, I'm working in ITRInow and can't afford so much time. In fact, if using the above configurationand ES is still cracked, then we get into a mess shit.If the root of coral needs 8lgm advisory or something else, you may contactme. If you guys wanna to catch the cracker, log every packet to coral andfilter the from IP address, and then catch catch catch.Just remember one thing: IF YOU DON'T WANT TO BE CRACKED, CLOSE THE PORTSand OPEN PORTS WHICH IS BADLY NEEDED.I'll try to hack coral after the process listed above completed, 'cause cracking a site needs only TWO HOURS!! If the site is secure, then just reopen ES. Yes, I said it, reopen.*NOTE* If you use ptelnet, the usrname can't exceed 7 chars, or it will be       unsecured.			Lilia the Queen stands here.Sorry to waste all of your time. *bow*"
